{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":403,"output":403,"cacheRead":8192,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":17,"totalTokens":8998,"cost":{"input":0.001209,"output":0.006045,"cacheRead":0.0024576,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0097116}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"All 8 tests pass. Summary:\n\n**Root cause** — `createEventProjector` chained every event onto one global `pending` promise. Once `applyToStore` rejected, that chain stayed rejected forever, poisoning all later events for every trade; the same global chain serialized unrelated trades behind each other. State was also written to the in-memory map *before* persistence succeeded, and there was no version/lifecycle/payload validation.\n\n**Repair** (in `benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/event-projector.mjs`):\n- Per-trade promise tails → serial per trade, concurrent across trades.\n- Tail continued with a rejection-swallowing handler so one failure never poisons later work.\n- `states.set` only after `await applyToStore(...)` succeeds.\n- Full validation: malformed events → `TypeError`; first event must be `CREATED` v1; exact `version + 1`; duplicate/stale versions return the current snapshot without persisting; `CANCELLED` is terminal; `CREATED` requires positive finite `notional` and non-empty `owner`, `AMENDED` must leave a valid complete state.\n- Deep clones on input, callback args, returns, and snapshots.\n\n**Tests added** (6 in `student-tests.mjs`): cross-trade concurrency while one trade is blocked, duplicate/stale no-op, gap/invalid-first rejection with recovery, cancelled terminal, malformed-event `TypeError`s, and mutation-isolation of inputs/outputs/snapshots.\n\n**Visible result**: `node --test …` → `pass 8, fail 0`.\n\n**Remaining risk** (also in `INCIDENT.md`): per-trade tails live in a `Map` for the projector's lifetime (minor memory growth with many distinct trade IDs); persistence failures are surfaced to the caller without retries by design."}}
